  "term": "reparameterization",
  "definition": "Reparameterization is a way of reorganizing part of a network so it can use features more efficiently while reducing computational load and memory use. In this packet, it refers to combining intrinsic and redundant features through a lightweight layer to improve speed and keep performance strong.",
